From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: At30c <173511395+At30c@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 19:25:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] bpf: accept newer program-load attributes for privileged
 loaders

Android 17's libbpf passes BPF_PROG_LOAD metadata fields added after Linux
4.19, including BTF function and line information.  The Exynos 990 kernel's
union bpf_attr ends at expected_attach_type, so bpf_check_uarg_tail_zero()
rejects these debug-only fields with E2BIG before the verifier sees the
program.

For privileged BPF_PROG_LOAD callers, accept a bounded newer attribute
structure and copy the prefix understood by this kernel.  The ignored tail
cannot change 4.19 verifier or runtime semantics, while map operations and
unprivileged program loads retain the strict tail check.  Log the compatibility
path once, and also log an actual instruction-count rejection so both E2BIG
sources remain distinguishable in pstore.
---
 kernel/bpf/syscall.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/bpf/syscall.c b/kernel/bpf/syscall.c
index 61a3e82f0501..d0d08b620868 100644
--- a/kernel/bpf/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/bpf/syscall.c
@@ -1410,8 +1410,11 @@ static int bpf_prog_load(union bpf_attr *attr)
 	/* eBPF programs must be GPL compatible to use GPL-ed functions */
 	is_gpl = license_is_gpl_compatible(license);
 
-	if (attr->insn_cnt == 0 || attr->insn_cnt > BPF_MAXINSNS)
+	if (attr->insn_cnt == 0 || attr->insn_cnt > BPF_MAXINSNS) {
+		pr_err("BPF_PROG_LOAD invalid instruction count: %u (max %u)\n",
+		       attr->insn_cnt, BPF_MAXINSNS);
 		return -E2BIG;
+	}
 
 	if (type == BPF_PROG_TYPE_KPROBE &&
 	    attr->kern_version != LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
@@ -2418,8 +2421,12 @@ SYSCALL_DEFINE3(bpf, int, cmd, union bpf_attr __user *, uattr, unsigned int, siz
 		return -EPERM;
 
 	err = bpf_check_uarg_tail_zero(uattr, sizeof(attr), size);
-	if (err)
+	if (err && !(cmd == BPF_PROG_LOAD && err == -E2BIG &&
+		    size <= 256 && capable(CAP_SYS_ADMIN)))
 		return err;
+	if (err)
+		pr_warn_once("BPF: accepting newer BPF_PROG_LOAD attribute tail (%u > %zu bytes)\n",
+			     size, sizeof(attr));
 	size = min_t(u32, size, sizeof(attr));
 
 	/* copy attributes from user space, may be less than sizeof(bpf_attr) */
-- 
2.43.0
